1	#!/usr/bin/env node
2	// The provenance log's one tool (the provenance design, #2136): every flow that
3	// creates or changes an element appends through it, the marking pass runs through it,
4	// and a maintainer checks a pack with it. Two roots - a canon's `packs/<id>` and a
5	// member's `.claudinite/local/packs/<id>` - resolved from the id, or `--all` for every
6	// pack under both. The grammar and the codemods are the engine helper's
7	// (engine/checks/helpers/provenance.mjs); this is the command line over them, and
8	// the parts that need git or a scrub.
9	//
10	//   node <path-to-this-file> mark <pack>|--all [--dry-run]
11	//   node <path-to-this-file> check <pack>|--all
12	//   node <path-to-this-file> convert-references <pack>|--all
13	//   node <path-to-this-file> append <pack> <element> [--kind <kind>] [--date <YYYY-MM-DD>] [--changed] < entry.md
14	//   node <path-to-this-file> reduce <file> [--public]
15	//   node <path-to-this-file> history <pack> <element>
16	//   node <path-to-this-file> brief <pack> [<element>…]
17	//   node <path-to-this-file> apply <pack> <brief.md>
18	//
